  "You've hit your session limit \u00b7 resets 10:50pm (Asia/Singapore)",
  "## Design\n\n**Strategy.** The player never moves left or right, so it stays in column 5 for the whole episode and only chooses no-op, up or down. Because the column is fixed, each row's threat or opportunity is a fixed function of that row's cells. The weights are hand-derived and untested, since nothing could be run.\n\nEach action gets a utility, and the large logit scale makes the softmax close to an argmax:\n\n- **Danger.** Each action is penalised by how soon the enemy in the row it leads to reaches column 5. An approaching enemy at distance \u22641 or on column 5 costs about 1000, distance 2 costs 300, distance 3 costs 60, distance 4 costs 10, distance 5 costs 4. A receding enemy costs 0. The player therefore leaves its row early, which gives several attempts against sticky no-ops.\n- **Sticky-move lookahead.** Up and down carry an extra cost (25 alone, much more combined with other danger) if the row two away has an enemy about to reach column 5, since a repeated move would carry the player into it.\n- **Treasure.** An approaching treasure at distance d from column 5 has reach d+1 rows. Each reachable treasure above adds +18 to up, each below adds +12 to down, and one approaching in the player's own row adds +40 to no-op.\n- **Housekeeping.** No-op has a +6 bias; rows 1\u20132 and 7\u20138 get a mild push back towards the centre; up at row 1 and down at row 8 are blocked; left, right and fire sit at \u22125000.\n\n**Layer 1 (31 units used).** Direction comes from the trail: each row's cost is an exact linear function of its enemy and trail cells, solved so that approaching gives the cost and receding gives 0.\n\n- Units 0\u20137, `Stay_r`: gated by \"player in row r\", output the danger of row r.\n- Units 8\u201314, `Up_r` (r=2..8): gated the same way, danger of row r\u22121 plus lookahead on row r\u22122.\n- Units 15\u201321, `Down_r` (r=1..7): danger of row r+1 plus lookahead on row r+2.\n- Units 22\u201329, `G_r`: treasure reach of row r, encoded as \u22121 + 0.25\u00b7reach (\u22121 if none or receding).\n- Unit 30: player row as a near-linear analogue value.\n\n**Layer 2 (30 units used).**\n\n- Units 0\u20132: linear pass-through of the summed stay, up and down costs.\n- Unit 3: player row pass-through.\n- Units 4\u20135: \"at row 1\" and \"at row 8\".\n- Units 6\u201312, `A_r`: true when player row \u2212 r \u2264 reach of row r (treasure above within reach).\n- Units 13\u201319, `B_r`: the same for treasure below.\n- Units 20\u201327: detect approaching treasure in the player's own row.\n- Units 28\u201329: \"row \u2264 2\" and \"row \u2265 7\".\n\n```edits\n# ================= LAYER 1 =================\nb1[0:22] = -24\nb1[22:30] = -5\n\n# ---- gates: player cell (row r, col 5) -> Stay_r, Up_r, Down_r ; analog row unit 30\nW1[90, 0] = 20\nW1[90, 15] = 20\nW1[90, 30] = -0.07\nW1[150, 1] = 20\nW1[150, 8] = 20\nW1[150, 16] = 20\nW1[150, 30] = -0.05\nW1[210, 2] = 20\nW1[210, 9] = 20\nW1[210, 17] = 20\nW1[210, 30] = -0.03\nW1[270, 3] = 20\nW1[270, 10] = 20\nW1[270, 18] = 20\nW1[270, 30] = -0.01\nW1[330, 4] = 20\nW1[330, 11] = 20\nW1[330, 19] = 20\nW1[330, 30] = 0.01\nW1[390, 5] = 20\nW1[390, 12] = 20\nW1[390, 20] = 20\nW1[390, 30] = 0.03\nW1[450, 6] = 20\nW1[450, 13] = 20\nW1[450, 21] = 20\nW1[450, 30] = 0.05\nW1[510, 7] = 20\nW1[510, 14] = 20\nW1[510, 30] = 0.07\n\n# ---- main danger of row q (enemy, gold, trail) -> Stay_q, Up_{q+1}, Down_{q-1}\n# row 1 -> units 0, 8\nW1[61:120:6, 0] = [1.241, 1.702, 3.865, 5.278, 11.865, 13.278, 11.865, 5.278, 3.865, 1.702]\nW1[62:120:6, 0] = [0, 0, 1.241, 1.702, 3.865, 5.278, 3.865, 1.702, 1.241, 0]\nW1[64:120:6, 0] = [0, -1.241, -1.702, -3.865, -5.278, -11.865, -5.278, -3.865, -1.702, -1.241]\nW1[61:120:6, 8] = [1.241, 1.702, 3.865, 5.278, 11.865, 13.278, 11.865, 5.278, 3.865, 1.702]\nW1[62:120:6, 8] = [0, 0, 1.241, 1.702, 3.865, 5.278, 3.865, 1.702, 1.241, 0]\nW1[64:120:6, 8] = [0, -1.241, -1.702, -3.865, -5.278, -11.865, -5.278, -3.865, -1.702, -1.241]\n# row 2 -> units 1, 9